% The self-attacking argument as a classical debate (lk copy of
% self_attack.fspy).  P from a presumed refutation of P.  Unfolding
% captures that presumption with P's own continuation, and since
% 2026-09-25 a captured presumption is a commitment the debate made, not
% an assumption, so what remains is the classical proof of P from
% (P->false)->P.  Strict in the debate, hence a strict edge SelfAttack*
% on the issue graph: P[t] IN, evaluation a VALUE in both modes.
lk.

# Rationality fixture: self-attack (odd loop of length 1).
# One argument for P resting on the negation-as-failure default for P itself:
# pRule needs P->false on the term side, derived from a geled for P.
# The FRAMEWORK alone still grounds P UNDEC on both sides - it cannot see
# that the capture discharged the site.  The strict phase can, and the
# issue graph is framework plus strict edges, so `label SelfAttack` shows
# P[t] IN.  Before 2026-09-25 the evaluation was OPEN.

declare P:bool.
declare pRule : ((P->false)->P).

start argument SelfAttack P
cut ((P->false)->P) rule.
axiom pRule.
elim.
elim h.
cut (P) alpha.
axiom h.
by default.
next.
axiom.
end argument

graph SelfAttack
label SelfAttack preferred
evaluate SelfAttack credulous
